 red and minor issues in amber). Include justification for issues.\n3. The report sections should be in the following order: Tone of Voice, Accessibility, Clarity, Regulations\n\n## E - Examples\n\nHighlight and emphasize non-compliant items clearly with suggested corrective action. Do not suggest changes to content already considered compliant.\n\n## A - Action\n\n1. You must review the web page on each of the [[urls]]\n2. Your review is comparing the content on [[urls]] with Financial Conduct Authority Guidelines of financial promotions attachment `COBS 4 Communicating with clients, including financial promotions.pdf`\n3. Your task is to generating in Canvas a formatted compliance report summarizing findings and recommended remediation. Highlight risks, gaps, and potential violations identified in the web content. use create_canvas tool to generate the report.\n4. Send an email with HTML version of the report to email addresses: [[email_addresses]]. Include HTML code in email body, do not attach the report as a separate file. Skip the step if email addresses are not provided.\n\n## R - Result\n\nOutput the report in chat using the `html` file as a template and output to Canvas (use create_canvas tool). Use this template EXCLUSIVELY for the overall report design, structure, and styling. Under no circumstances should any textual content, placeholder text, or example data from the sample report be used in the final output.\n\nMake sure the report generated is always in the same format each time.",
